WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.200
-As always, you look great.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.234
You're a stud.
They love you. We love you.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:07.033
Welcome back. Come on.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.501
-We have a thousand things
to talk about.

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:09.501
-Do we?
-Yes.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.100
-Okay.
-Last time you were here,

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.968
you were engaged.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.834
Now officially,
you are married.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:16.601
Congratulations.
That's the great thing.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:20.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.868
How was the wedding?
How was everybody?

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.033
-Honestly?
-Yeah.

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:25.934
-It was pretty seamless.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.667
Like everybody,
friends and family warned us.

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.200
They were like,
"Just be prepared.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.434
Something's going to go wrong.
That's fine.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.767
You know, just let it
roll off your shoulder."

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.133
-Yes.
-But honestly,

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.200
nothing went wrong.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.067
It was perfect.
-Really?

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:41.467
-It was -- You know, we did it
at a place we loved.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.834
Little wine country,
pretty close to where we live.

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:46.267
-Big wedding?
-I would say

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.100
on the smaller side.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.934
It was like just under 100.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:52.434
-That's perfect.
-It was. It was perfect.

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.400
-And how long now
have you been married?

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.934
-Well, in...
-Uh-oh.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:58.634
-Right? Oh, dang!

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.701
-Here's where it all went wrong.
I'm so sorry.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.467
-No, I'm just trying to do math.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:05.467
-Okay. Wedding was 11/11, so...
-Almost a year.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.434
-Yeah. Less than -- Yeah.
In less than two weeks,

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:09.634
we'll have our one-year
anniversary.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.167
-Wow. Hey!
I'm so happy for you, buddy.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.434
-Thank you.

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.334
-You're co-hosting
with your wife

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:19.067
this podcast
called "The Squeeze,"

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:21.167
and it is streaming now.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:24.033
I love that her name
is Taylor as well.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.234
-Yeah.
-And so she became

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:26.767
Taylor Lautner when she got
married to you.

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:28.334
-Yes, I know.

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.200
-I think it's great.
-Do you?

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.100
-Yes.
-It's quite narcissistic.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.434
-I love it actually.
I think it's fantastic.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:35.901
I do want to hear
about "The Squeeze" too.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:38.000
And tell everyone the reason
behind the name, "The Squeeze."

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.000
And what is the idea
behind the podcast?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.300
-The short version is we both

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.667
are passionate
about mental health,

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:48.734
and the podcast is
a mental-health-based podcast.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:52.634
My wife was a nurse
through COVID.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.067
-Wow.
-And kind of --

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:59.534
-Thank you.
-Yeah, she's incredible.

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:04.267
But after going through that,
she --

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.901
she realized
that she had to take a step back

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.334
to kind of prioritize
her mental health.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:12.534
She deals with a lot
of that stuff still today.

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:15.934
And we kind of just started both
of our mental-health journeys

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:18.133
around the same time.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.100
Me realizing I had to just,
like,

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.601
address things
that I just pushed down

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:24.901
and never really thought about,

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:27.868
just the way that I grew up
being in the spotlight

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.734
since a kid.

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:33.133
And I just never -- I never
thought about it that way.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.434
And I was like, you know what?

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.634
I need to, like,
take this seriously.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:40.133
And we started that together.
So it was really awesome

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:42.100
to have each other
going through that journey.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.734
This was, you know,
right around COVID time,

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:47.934
you know, kind of like
the journey for many of us.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:52.767
-Yeah.
-And from that we were like,

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:55.234
we feel called
to do this podcast

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:59.701
and just have vulnerable
conversations with ourselves,

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.434
our guests, so...

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:05.501
-And then "The Squeeze" is...?
-"The Squeeze"

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.968
is just the juice
of your mental health.

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.267
-Yeah. The squeeze.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:12.601
-Yes. We get into it.
We don't hold back.

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:15.100
-Yeah. Life gives you lemons.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.334
-Yeah.
-Make lemonade.

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.934
-Yes. Absolutely.
That's what we're trying to do.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.267
-Yeah.
-It's not easy.

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:22.701
-No. That's fantastic that
you're doing this.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.868
I mean,
I'm sure you've learned a lot.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:27.868
I mean, since you started this,
I mean, you talk to experts

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:29.501
and you talk to all these --
It's just --

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.200
And people that are
experiencing this stuff.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.601
It's great that you're putting
it out there and doing this.

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:36.033
I want to talk to you
about an unexpected call

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.868
that you got not too long ago

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:40.968
about you starring
in a Taylor Swift music video.

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:41.834
-Yes.

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:43.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:48.734
-It was awesome. It was so fun.
Talk about this.

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:50.133
Where were you?
Where did it happen?

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:53.000
-Oh, my goodness,
I was at home.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.601
It was like a morning
around 9 a.m.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:59.567
I get a call from my manager
and he goes,

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:02.067
"You will never believe who I
got a call from this morning."

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:04.701
And I go, "I wouldn't,
so why don't you tell me?"

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:07.567
And he goes,
"Taylor Swift's manager.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:10.000
And she wants to see
if she can get

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.534
your new updated cellphone
number and reach out."

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:15.634
I was like..."O-kay.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.167
Did they say what about?"

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:20.167
He's like, "Not really."
I'm like, "Okay."

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.067
He goes, "Do you want to talk
to your wife about this?

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:25.634
Make sure it's okay?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:28.868
Meanwhile, wife is like
right in the kitchen there

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.100
and she's freaking out.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.968
And I go, "No,
by the signs of it,

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.534
I think she's going to be
just fine."

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:36.667
She's the biggest Swifty ever.

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:41.200
So, automatic permission.
And then yeah,

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.968
Taylor reached out,
pitched me the idea.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.968
The idea was incredible.

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.734
-And you guys
had known each other?

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:50.501
-Yeah. Yeah, but we had been
out of touch for a while,

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:55.133
so it was a real cool,
full-circle moment

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:58.667
for both of us, and then we

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:02.534
jetted off to Liverpool,
England, shot the video.

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:03.667
-Why Liverpool?

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:05.400
-We were going
to do it in London.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.234
But then, you know, she's
experienced at these things.

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:09.868
She realized there
would probably be too many

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.767
like paparazzi and media

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.868
because we wanted
to keep it a secret.

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:15.434
-Yeah, of course.
-For the big reveal.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:16.868
-It was a great surprise.

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:18.300
-It was. It turned out perfect.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.400
-It was unbelievable.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.100
I loved it,
but then she premiered it,

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:24.067
I want to say, in Kansas City.
-Yes.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.968
Yeah.
So after we finished filming,

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:29.434
a couple of months go by
and she's like, "No pressure.

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:30.834
I got this crazy idea.

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:33.801
I was thinking, you know,
the night that my album drops,

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:38.033
just blind premiering it
at my show in Kansas City,

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.634
and people are going to freak.

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:42.434
They're going to faint. Like,
it's going to be unbelievable.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:46.300
And then after we show
the video, you and the cast

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.100
are going to walk out
and you'll actually be there."

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.133
I was like, "Sign me up."
So we did.

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:53.534
-But wait, but let me
just tell you something.

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:55.901
Not only did you come out
and make an entrance,

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:57.901
you made quite the entrance.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:06:00.200
-This is so ridiculous.
-No, this is my favorite.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.901
You know it.
We all saw it and we love it.

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:05.300
But I want to show if anyone
didn't see Taylor Lautner,

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.367
here's him making an entrance
at the concert.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.334
Look at this.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.701
-Tay-Tay, do you want to
come out?

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:12.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:16.167
Oh, no. Aaaaaaah!

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:17.367
[ Applause ]

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:20.234
-Did you -- First of all --

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:23.501
First of all, that's amazing.
Were you nervous at all

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:24.968
for a second and go like,
"What am I doing?

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:27.067
I'm not going to do
a flip" or what --

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:29.300
What went through your mind?

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:33.067
-I know. I do this weird thing
and it doesn't make sense,

00:06:33.067 --> 00:06:34.634
so forgive me.

00:06:34.634 --> 00:06:37.901
But when I freak out
and I'm really nervous

00:06:37.901 --> 00:06:42.033
and I black out,
I just go straight to backflip.

00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:43.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:48.667
So I stepped out of this door
and I saw this, like, this,

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:50.267
whatever, this walkway.

00:06:50.267 --> 00:06:53.200
And it was like 60 yards
down the field.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.834
And I'm like, "I have to walk
down this whole thing?

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:56.968
This is going to be
so uncomfortable."

00:06:56.968 --> 00:06:58.734
I was like, "Just backflip,

00:06:58.734 --> 00:07:01.400
and I'll take up the space
and it'll be over."

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:06.767
-It was awesome.
That could have gone so wrong.

00:07:06.767 --> 00:07:08.734
-Oh, it could have.
-It could have gone so wrong.

00:07:08.734 --> 00:07:11.000
And it went so right.
Well done, buddy.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.400
-Thank you.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.133
-In the video, by the way,
you do some epic fight scenes

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:19.033
and I read somewhere
that Taylor Swift

00:07:19.033 --> 00:07:20.968
knew you pretty well,
so she was like,

00:07:20.968 --> 00:07:23.367
"No, I know that Taylor Lautner
can do these stunts."

00:07:23.367 --> 00:07:25.534
You did your own stunts
for a lot of these movies.

00:07:25.534 --> 00:07:27.033
She's like, "No,
he knows how to do this."

00:07:27.033 --> 00:07:29.033
-Yeah.
-Do you know how to do that?

00:07:29.033 --> 00:07:31.834
And did I know that you knew
how to do that?

00:07:31.834 --> 00:07:34.934
-I don't know, but yeah,

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:38.501
she knew
of my martial arts background.

00:07:38.501 --> 00:07:39.634
She's just incredible.

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:42.934
So I trusted her
with everything. But yeah.

00:07:42.934 --> 00:07:45.434
-Could you show me a move?
-Could I show you a move?

00:07:45.434 --> 00:07:47.834
-I mean, I don't know.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:49.701
Is there a move
that I could learn?

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:51.534
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:51.534 --> 00:07:53.934
Okay. Yeah, I got an idea.

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:55.934
So there was a move
I did in the video,

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:58.634
but there's
a simpler version of it

00:07:58.634 --> 00:08:00.567
and that's called
a tornado kick.

00:08:00.567 --> 00:08:02.868
And I think -- I think you're
going to be able to do this.

00:08:02.868 --> 00:08:04.200
-Alright.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.734
-What do I do? That sounds --
-Okay.

00:08:05.734 --> 00:08:07.801
So I'll take you step by step.
-Yeah.

00:08:07.801 --> 00:08:11.267
-So I'm going to show you
like a slow version first.

00:08:11.267 --> 00:08:13.067
So here.
-Am I going to be okay here?

00:08:13.067 --> 00:08:15.234
-You're going to go --
Yeah. Come on up.

00:08:15.234 --> 00:08:18.100
You can walk through
this first part with me.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.367
-I don't want to step
into the tornado.

00:08:20.367 --> 00:08:22.000
-I'm not going to do it
full out right now.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.701
-Alright.
-We're going to take it
slow first.

00:08:23.701 --> 00:08:25.100
-Yes.
-So just face this way.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.634
-Okay.
-With your left foot,

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.767
you're going to go step

00:08:28.767 --> 00:08:32.968
and then right foot's
going to come around here.

00:08:32.968 --> 00:08:35.934
Left foot knee
is going to go up.

00:08:35.934 --> 00:08:39.067
And then the right foot
is going to kick.

00:08:39.067 --> 00:08:40.667
So when you put it together

00:08:40.667 --> 00:08:41.901
I'll show you
what that looks like.

00:08:41.901 --> 00:08:45.300
So it's step,
turn, left, kick.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.133
So it's tornado kick, step,
turn, left, kick.

00:08:48.133 --> 00:08:51.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:51.968 --> 00:08:53.734
I think you got it.

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:55.968
I think you got it.
-I know step, turn.

00:08:55.968 --> 00:09:00.100
-Step, turn, left leg comes up,
and the right one kicks.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.734
-Step, turn.
-Left up and kick.

00:09:02.734 --> 00:09:04.100
Yes, that's going to be it.
You got it.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.367
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:09.334
Turn left.

00:09:09.334 --> 00:09:14.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:14.734 --> 00:09:16.434
-Do we have to see it
in slow mo?

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:18.501
Do I have to watch it
in slow mo?

00:09:18.501 --> 00:09:20.868
Let's just watch.
This is sad. Look at grandpa.

00:09:20.868 --> 00:09:24.300
Ahhhhhhhhh, aaah, oh!

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:27.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:30.801
Fell down.
-You got that leg up there.

00:09:30.801 --> 00:09:32.334
-Taylor Lautner, everybody.

00:09:32.334 --> 00:09:38.133
His podcast,
"The Squeeze," is streaming now.

00:09:38.133 --> 00:09:39.567
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:09:39.567 --> 00:09:41.467
Stick around, everybody.
Come on.

